<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38168" root="ليث" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَيَّثٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِلْيَثٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  (tropical:)  A <i>strong</i> stallion; likened
to a lion. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَيَّبٌ</span> <i>Fat, and broken,</i> or
<i>trained, to obedience;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمِينٌ مُذَلَّلٌ</span>. (TS,
K.) [See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لوث</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكَانٌ مُلَيَّثٌ</span>,
as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَوَّثٌ</span>, <i>A place having dry herbage,
and being rained upon, and producing fresh
herbage, so that half of it is green, and half
of it yellow.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَأْسٌ مُلَيَّثٌ</span>, as also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَوَّثٌ</span>, <i>A head of which part of the hair is
black, and part white.</i> (TA.)

